Third-party data
----------------

Some source files contain tables generated from Unicode data: character properties from the Unicode Character
Database (through Python's unicodedata module) and plural rules, language, script and territory codes from the
Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR, through the Babel library). These tables are covered by the Unicode
License v3, reproduced below. Other tables record the byte mappings of standard code pages and character sets as
Python's codecs implement them.

bilingua-pdf follows the text extraction rules of PDFium and its source holds tables taken from PDFium, from
Adobe's glyph list and from Adobe's core 14 AFM font metrics:
- PDFium: Copyright 2014 The PDFium Authors (original code copyright 2014 Foxit Software Inc.), BSD 3-Clause
  licence, reproduced verbatim below.
- Adobe Glyph List: Copyright 1997-2010 Adobe Systems Incorporated, BSD 3-Clause licence, reproduced below.
- The AFM metrics carry Adobe's AFM notice, which bilingua-pdf/src/tables.rs keeps unmodified with the data.

The source repository's test folders (not the published packages) also hold test files from the Okapi Framework,
which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; each such folder lists them.

